-- Imported TDB 434 spawns duplicated the native NPCs: TDB and the 3.3.5a database place the same
-- NPC up to a hub apart, so the 0.5 m import dedupe missed them and the landing added a second copy
-- (#272). Delete the imported copy that stands within 100 m of its native twin; spawn import now
-- dedupes at that radius and maps the skipped spawn's scripts to the surviving twin.
-- Placements further away are separate locations and are kept. The spawns that carry GUID-specific
-- behavior (SmartAI, addon, formation, game event) are kept too: the twin cannot inherit it.
-- Statements filter on `id` and `guid`: the linter rejects spawn deletes that only name one of them.
